From 9da8ff53f751f6682f69897d886f3a9946deed31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Sephton <matt.sephton@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 19:40:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ppa): decide engine idleness under the engine spinlock

Merges https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf/pull/19047

The engine's "idle" state was a binary semaphore that the completion ISR
gave only AFTER leaving the engine spinlock, while ppa_do_operation
inserted its transaction under that spinlock and then tried the semaphore
with a zero timeout. On the ISR's own core the two cannot interleave. When
the submitting task runs on the OTHER core it can insert between the
ISR's "queue empty" decision and its give, find the semaphore still taken,
assume the ISR will chain-start the transaction, and be left at the head of
an idle engine's queue. It only starts when a later submission's completion
picks it up; a lone last submission never completes and a caller waiting on
its done callback blocks forever.

Seen on ESP32-P4 with the PPA/2D-DMA interrupt on core 0 and SRM
transactions submitted from a core-1 task: ~130 stranded transactions per
20000 when single transactions are submitted at their own duration, none
when the submitter is on core 0; none after this change.

Replace the semaphore with a `busy` flag that both sides read and write
only under the engine spinlock: the submitter inserts and, if the engine
is idle, marks it busy and starts the transaction itself; the ISR clears
the flag in the same critical section in which it finds the queue empty.
Blocking mode also clears a stale give on the recycled per-transaction
semaphore (the ISR gives it unconditionally, non-blocking callers never
take it), which made a blocking operation return before its transaction
had finished.
